nodecode-ordaprompt is a rewrite of aska-digital's aska-digital/protean-ordaprompt:

  https://github.com/aska-digital/protean-ordaprompt
  commit 60e89af2853072c7801c465f30999f3c6ceb35b2
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 aska-digital (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the routing policy of ordaprompt_router/router.py -- one batch
comparison per surface, the three bands with their thresholds and margins, the
novel and ambiguity sentinels, session utility with its context cost and
contamination risk, the effective band as the more conservative of the two,
the escalation codes, the closed contamination weights, and the decision
values; the receipt shape and its hashes-only promise from receipts.py and
schemas.py; and the two verbs of cli.py, as the ordaprompt_route tool and the
/ordaprompt command.

Left out, and why: the SyntheticBackend that scored a prompt by hashing it was
the fixture backend, deterministic but blind to what the prompt said, so the
cell scores by words instead and keeps every band above that score unchanged;
the OpenRouter adapter (disabled by default, hashes-only taxonomy proposals)
has no key to set and no proposal to make here, so a novel ask answers
novel_propose and leaves the naming to the caller; the CalibrationModel and
the eval harness existed to prove the error gate on synthetic fixtures, and the
single calibration_active switch carries what they decided; the Hermes
directory-plugin wrapper (__init__.py, plugin.yaml, a no-op register()) has no
Nodecode counterpart, since a cell declares its section, tool and command in
one form; and the argparse CLI became the tool's argument contract.
